      "severity": "BLOCKING_PHYSICS_SIGN_BUG",
      "summary": "Wrong sign in 1-loop 5-flavor QED top-quark decoupling alpha_EM^-1(5)(M_Z). Because d(alpha_EM^-1)/d(ln mu) = -b_EM/(2 pi) and decoupling the top quark lowers b_EM by Delta b_EM = (4/3)*N_c*Q_t^2 = +16/9, running downward from mu=m_t to mu=M_Z reduces QED screening, so alpha_EM^-1(5)(M_Z) = alpha_EM^-1(6)(M_Z) - (16/9)/(2 pi)*ln(m_t/M_Z) < alpha_EM^-1(6)(M_Z) (matching line 1090 sparticle decoupling minus sign and standard MSbar decoupling +2/(3 pi) N_c Q_t^2 ln(M_Z/m_t)). Producer wrote '+' instead of '-', producing alpha_EM^-1(5) > alpha_EM^-1(6) with rel err up to 3.59e-3 (~0.452 in alpha_EM^-1) across all OW27-A runs, OW27-D LINK6/HYBRID, B4_UV_MZ_BLIND_LOCK_V3, and A2-OW16 v20 OBS-08. Flipping only that sign reduces residual against producer from 3.59e-3 to < 1e-7."
